# QA evidence: 204 screenshots, 82 MB — 90% of this folder by size and 70% by
# file count. It is all regenerable from the harnesses, none of it is deployed,
# and in a repo it would make every clone slow forever to no benefit. The README's
# "QA" section describes what was asserted; the images stay local.
# Delete this line if you ever want the trail in version control.
_qa/

# Python bytecode from the build scripts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local previews / harness leftovers. `check-deploy.py` fails the build if any of
# these end up in site/, but they should not reach git either.
cdp-profile/
*.log
*.orig
*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOT ignored, on purpose:
#   site/        — this is the deployable. Netlify publishes it, and the GitHub
#                  Action commits regenerated pages into it. Ignoring it would
#                  deploy an empty site.
#   build/raw/   — the ungraded generated forest frames (~6 MB). They are the only
#                  copy: re-running the generator is a fresh dice throw and the
#                  old frame is gone. Cheap insurance.
#   build/google-reviews.json — the review archive. Committing it is the whole
#                  reason the refresh runs in Actions rather than on a build hook.
